 "dur": 45.137,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why were history's first pilots a sheep, a duck, and a rooster?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.992
  },
  {
   "text": "Their basket rises under a giant balloon. Nobody knows if the sky will kill them.",
   "s": 3.292,
   "e": 7.684
  },
  {
   "text": "Below, 130,000 people are watching, including the king.",
   "s": 7.884,
   "e": 11.517
  },
  {
   "text": "Scientists warned that the air up high could be poison.",
   "s": 11.717,
   "e": 14.001
  },
  {
   "text": "So the balloon gets filled with smoke from burning straw, wool, and old shoes.",
   "s": 14.201,
   "e": 17.953
  },
  {
   "text": "But it shoots up so fast the crowd screams, and a gust rips the cloth!",
   "s": 18.153,
   "e": 21.215
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it drifts away, two miles, and vanishes behind a forest.",
   "s": 21.415,
   "e": 24.382
  },
  {
   "text": "So why send farm animals first?",
   "s": 24.582,
   "e": 26.207
  },
  {
   "text": "The sheep breathes like us. The duck already flies high. The rooster? In between.",
   "s": 26.507,
   "e": 30.279
  },
  {
   "text": "If all three come back fine, the sky is safe for humans.",
   "s": 30.479,
   "e": 33.258
  },
  {
   "text": "Riders gallop into the forest, and find the basket.",
   "s": 33.658,
   "e": 35.989
  },
  {
   "text": "The sheep is munching grass. The duck is fine. The rooster is grumpy: the sheep sat on him.",
   "s": 36.189,
   "e": 41.027
  },
  {
   "text": "Two months later, humans flew. But the sheep went first.",
   "s": 41.227,
   "e": 43.837
  }
 ],
